Z||000006||BBBAD GT||04-16-2001||01:29 PM||||It sure looks good.  Make sure you get a photo shoot when the new lowered suspension goes on, I always wanted to see what it looked like 'lowered'.  <P>Was this before the rear accident?  Its looks good if it was and you only repaired it.  Get the clutch MC problem fixed?  <P>I still think the wheels were made for that car.....<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jaei Sun||04-16-2001||03:15 PM||||Thanks for all the compliments... I was thinking the same to myself when I loaded them off the camera and on to the computer.  They turned out much better than I expected.<P>Standard - Snowing today... argh!  What gives.  Well it's back to drivin the Beretta for a few more days  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Jeff - I got the springs and now I'm waitin to get the struts/ shocks... most likely will be lowered in 2 weeks.  The was after the accident.  You can't even tell at all, I made just like new!<P>I re-bled the system and replaced the DOT3 with DOT4, and that helped.  I'll be getting a new GM Master and Slave in the summer. It works better now... not perfect, the new master and slave should make it 100%.||||reg||1
